{"commit_id":"6bc1218809a6faf83bc266c7a10b6b096f814a74","body":"A few things on the budget reader.","event":"COMMENT","comments":[{"path":"testdata/fixture/sample.go","side":"RIGHT","body":"This returns os.ReadFile's error with no context, so the caller sees a bare `no such file or directory` and cannot tell which budget failed. Wrap it: `fmt.Errorf(\"reading %s: %w\", path, err)`.","line":19},{"path":"testdata/fixture/sample.go","side":"RIGHT","start_side":"RIGHT","body":"A line that does not parse is skipped silently, so a typo in the budget file reads as a smaller total rather than as an error. Return the failure instead of continuing past it.","line":28,"start_line":25},{"path":"testdata/fixture/sample.go","side":"RIGHT","body":"A budget that really does total zero is reported as empty. Check whether any entry parsed instead of checking the total.","line":33}]}
